.TH SDL_SetMemoryFunctions 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_SetMemoryFunctions \- Replace SDL\(aqs memory allocation functions with a custom set.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_SetMemoryFunctions(SDL_malloc_func malloc_func,
.BI "                            SDL_calloc_func calloc_func,
.BI "                            SDL_realloc_func realloc_func,
.BI "                            SDL_free_func free_func);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
It is not safe to call this function once any allocations have been made, as future calls to
.BR SDL_free
will use the new allocator, even if they came from an
.BR SDL_malloc
made with the old one!
.PP
If used, usually this needs to be the first call made into the SDL library, if not the very first thing done at program startup time\[char46]
.PP
It is legal to call this with all 4 parameters set to NULL, which will restore the original memory functions without having to query them with
.BR SDL_GetOriginalMemoryFunctions ()
first\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I malloc_func
custom malloc function\[char46]
.TP
.I calloc_func
custom calloc function\[char46]
.TP
.I realloc_func
custom realloc function\[char46]
.TP
.I free_func
custom free function\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure\[char46] This only fails if there is a mix of NULL and non-NULL parameters\[char46] Failure will not set an error message (which allocates memory) so do _not_ call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
in response to a failure here\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread, but one should not replace the memory functions once any allocations are made!

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GetMemoryFunctions (3),
.BR SDL_GetOriginalMemoryFunctions (3)
